###  https://w3id.org/heritagegraph/FearlessnessAssessment
<https://w3id.org/heritagegraph/FearlessnessAssessment> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                        rdfs:subClassOf <https://w3id.org/heritagegraph/RitualAssessment> ;
                                                        rdfs:label "Fearlessness Assessment"@en ;
                                                        <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The 'fearlessness test' popularly described (animal heads, masked dancers in darkness). Its historical and contemporary practice is DISPUTED -- some former Kumaris contest how it is described. Represented as an assessment whose accounts are source-attributed via has_assertion, NOT as a mandatory criterion."@en ;
                                                        <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://w3id.org/heritagegraph/schema> ;
                                                        <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Deliberately not a SelectionCriterion subclass: popular accounts and lived testimony disagree. Attach each account as a Assertion (CRMinf I2 Belief) with its own source and confidence."@en .


